Maybe...:-)
Did you use "burn image" from the "file" menu in Nero?
Sorry for asking silly questions, but booting off a debian CD normally 
works.
As an alternative you may want to start installing from floppy disks. 
You just need the rescue-floppy for booting and the root disk. For the 
packages, you may then use your CD or install from the net.

 > Since Redhat doesn't seem to support Alpha anymore, I wanted to try a
 > current linux distribution that does and downloaded all 7
Woody is the current stable distro, but you may not find it to be a 
"current" distribution. In debian no new versions of packages enter the 
stable distribution no more; since woody was released a while ago, the 
packages aren't among the youngest no more. You may want to try 
"testing" or "unstable", which are more up to date.

Regards, Adrian.



